A||N||10||maninblack||reset ecm||||5||
Z||000000||maninblack||09-15-2000||04:10 AM||||I have replaced a new tps senor as of code 21<BR>,do i have to reset the ecm?,if i dont would it still "think" somthing is worng and try to corred the problem bu adjusting the tbs sensor?.<BR>thx||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||09-15-2000||07:49 AM||||Resetting the ECM is quite easy.  Disconnect the battery for 30 seconds or so.  Then all the stored codes get cleared and you can start fresh.  The car may run crappy at first, but once the ECM learns from all the sensors it will run as is should..provided everything is working as it should.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||09-15-2000||12:02 PM||||The ECM will remember all errors until reset.<P>Look for an orange wire in the harness near the battery. It should have a disconnect in it about 4-8 inches from the main terminal block on the fender wall. It's usually easy to find. All years have it far as I know. Not sure if it's in the same place on 84's.<P>If you undo that connection in the orange wire it will reset the ECM without wiping the radio.<P>The rest is pretty much like Lar said. It will run and idle weird untill you go for a drive. The idle will settle down once you drive over 35 for a mile or so. The rest may take a couple days to really settle in.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 09-15-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||maninblack||09-15-2000||12:29 PM||||thank you both for the information,i will do it right now  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||14
